---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import RiskVisual from '../components/RiskVisual.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  lang="en"
  title="CausaVera — Business Risk Intelligence"
  description="CausaVera connects services, systems, applications, controls, evidence and obligations to business impact and risk."
>
  <header class="container header">
    <a class="brand" href="/">CausaVera</a>
    <nav class="nav">
      <a href="#approach">How we think</a>
      <a href="#insights">Insights</a>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a class="lang" href="/fr/">FR</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Business Risk Intelligence</span>
      <h1>See what technology risk means to the business.</h1>
      <p>
        CausaVera connects business services, systems, applications, controls,
        obligations, expected evidence and control effectiveness so leaders can
        understand what matters, why it matters, and where attention belongs.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="#approach">Explore the approach</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#insights">Read the research</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <RiskVisual />

    <section id="approach" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Compliance is not the destination.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A control failure, vulnerability or compliance issue is only the beginning of the question.
          CausaVera is designed to connect that condition to the business service it can affect,
          the evidence expected, the control's effectiveness, and the resulting business consequence.
        </p>
        <div class="grid-3">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Start with the business</h3>
            <p>Anchor technology and controls to the services the organization actually depends on.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Connect the control story</h3>
            <p>Bring obligations, expected evidence and control effectiveness into one understandable chain.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Make risk decision-ready</h3>
            <p>Translate technical conditions into context that executives, risk teams and operators can act on.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="insights" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Insights & research</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          CausaVera's bilingual article series explores the gap between traditional compliance reporting
          and decision-ready business risk intelligence.
        </p>
        <div class="pdf-list">
          <div class="pdf-item">
            <strong>Article 01</strong>
            <div>
              <strong>Business Risk Intelligence</strong><br />
              <small>English and French publication pair</small>
            </div>
            <span class="status">Preparing release</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pdf-item">
            <strong>Series</strong>
            <div>
              <strong>12-part market education library</strong><br />
              <small>Paired bilingual PDFs will be published here as they are approved.</small>
            </div>
            <span class="status">In review</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>From findings to business meaning.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          CausaVera is being built to help organizations reason across the complete chain:
          Business Service → Systems → Applications → Controls → Obligations → Expected Evidence →
          Control Effectiveness → Business Impact / Risk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="container footer">
    CausaVera — Business Risk Intelligence.
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
